          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q U E S T I O N S"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.101,
            0.136,
            0.751,
            0.168
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. A ray of light travelling in air enters obliquely into water. Does the light ray bend towards the normal or away from the normal? Why?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.172,
            0.749,
            0.205
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Light enters from air to glass having refractive index 1.50. What is the",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " speed of light in the glass? The speed of light in vacuum is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 \\times 1 0 ^ { 8 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "m s",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "–1",
              "styles": [
                "bold",
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.1,
            0.209,
            0.75,
            0.241
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Find out, from Table 9.3, the medium having highest optical density. Also find the medium with lowest optical density.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.1,
            0.244,
            0.751,
            0.277
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. You are given kerosene, turpentine and water. In which of these does the light travel fastest? Use the information given in Table 9.3.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.101,
            0.281,
            0.75,
            0.312
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. The refractive index of diamond is 2.42. What is the meaning of this statement?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.772,
            0.172,
            0.894,
            0.318
          ],
          "content": [
            {
